WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.649
Children who experience physical, cognitive
or emotional neglect, say because their mother

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:12.179
was sick and their father was busy, often
face anxiety. As a result, their body produces

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:18.140
stress hormones. If this happens a lot, these
hormones become toxic for their developing

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:25.790
brain, which then later can repress emotional
and cognitive well-being for life.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:31.420
The real story of Daniel Rucareanu, who spent
part of his early childhood in a Romanian

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:40.260
orphanage, shows the full impact neglect can
have.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.690
The story began in 1966 when Romania’s then
leader, Nicolae Ceaușescu, wanted to make

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:52.850
his country a world powerhouse and came up
with laws to increase the country's population.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:58.630
Abortion and contraception were declared mostly
illegal. While the law led to a rapid rise

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:03.930
in birth rates, many of the poorer families
were unable to take care of all their children

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:11.579
and Daniel, and around half a million others,
were sent to state-run institutions.

00:01:11.579 --> 00:01:17.549
In most orphanages there were no toys, no
books, or anything else to stimulate cognitive

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:22.869
development. Many kids just stared at the
bare ceilings, waiting for their next meal.

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:29.029
Due to the lack of human contact, some babies
developed strategies for self stimulation,

00:01:29.029 --> 00:01:33.709
such as rocking back and forth.

00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:39.430
The cognitive neglect often led to lower IQ
scores, delayed language development and a

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:45.130
lack of creative thinking. This happens because
our brains build connections with every new

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:51.029
experience and stimulation. If there are no
rich experiences during the first years of

00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:56.130
life — the period in which the brain develops
the fastest — children cannot build the

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:03.819
foundations necessary for optimal future learning.
They miss out for life.

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:08.959
Daniel lived with over 400 other children
and their shared bedrooms were hardly ever

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:14.940
cleaned. The meals were mostly tiny portions
of boiled cabbage, which the staff would sometimes

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:21.291
steal to eat themselves. Some supervisors
used violence to control the orphans. Others

00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:29.170
encouraged the older kids to beat Daniel to
humiliate him and exercise authority..

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:34.409
The consequences of physical neglect and lack
of basic nutrients caused most orphans to

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:40.870
suffer from stunted growth. Some children
contracted HIV and Hepatitis B as a result

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:50.180
of the reusing of medical supplies. The physical
abuse caused severe bruising and other injuries.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:55.840
The overworked and under-trained staff hardly
ever soothed the crying children. In fact

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.270
they barely spent any time with Daniel at
all. Some children were left completely alone

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.959
with their worries, others hid their feelings
from the very people who ought to protect

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:11.390
them, since they feared being hurt.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:16.430
Emotional neglect and anxiety lead to an excessive
production of the stress hormones known as

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:22.111
adrenaline and cortisol,which is like poison
for the developing brain.But the experience

00:03:22.111 --> 00:03:27.920
also distorted the children’s understanding
of love and human relationships. They learned

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:37.069
to trust nobody and as adults, often suffered
from depression, insomnia and social anxiety.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:42.170
When Ceausescu's regime was eventually overthrown
and the conditions inside the orphanages were

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:48.250
shown on television, researchers from around
the world came to examine the nameless children.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:54.310
MRI scans later showed that some had smaller
volumes of brain mass. The resulting research

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:59.980
made a strong case that not only is nutrition
vital to a child's development, but so is

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:08.550
human contact. To help the children, a large
number were adopted into foreign families.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:14.700
But even after being adopted, many had problems
forming loving bonds to their new parents.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:19.250
This aligns with the attachment theory and
the notion that a child needs to establish

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:25.310
a loving relationship with at least one primary
caregiver early in life. Daniel was quite

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:31.130
lucky with his family. While he continued
to experience trauma and anxiety, he went

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:37.410
on to have a university education, started
a family of his own and later he founded a

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.980
non-profit organization for neglected children.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:49.440
If you grew up in a loving environment, count
yourself really, really lucky. If you experienced

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:55.380
forms of neglect, try to internalize the idea
that it was never your fault and maybe not

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.030
even your parents' fault either.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:03.320
To read what we think can be done if you have
ever experienced neglect, read the descriptions

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:24.850
below. One way is to share your thoughts about
neglect and how you think it affects you today.

